  ('banff-canada', '13A', 'Banff', 'Canada', 'The Rockies with a railway town at their feet', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Rockies', '{"ski","hiking","wellness","family"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["The FCDO names no advisory against travel anywhere in Canada; its alert_status field is empty. Source: gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/canada, reviewed 2026-06-02, read 2026-08-20.","4,515,000 visitors in 2025 — the highest to date, 7.14% above 2024; peak-summer visitation up 9%. Source: Parks Canada, Banff National Park Annual Report 2025.","Moraine Lake Road is closed to personal vehicles year-round. Source: parks.canada.ca Banff bulletin, read 2026-08-20.","Shuttle reservations opened 15 April 2026 at 8am MDT; 40% of seats released that day, 60% at 8am MDT two days before departure. Source: parks.canada.ca, read 2026-08-20.","The Canada Strong Pass with Parks Canada ends 7 September 2026; a valid pass is required from 8 September. Source: parks.canada.ca Banff fees, modified 2026-02-12.","Roam Public Transit carried 2,294,048 passengers in the park in 2025, up 12% on 2024. Source: Parks Canada Banff Annual Report 2025.","SkiBig3 spans 7,948 acres across Banff Sunshine Village, Lake Louise Ski Resort and Mt Norquay, with 2 gondolas and 32 chairlifts; Lake Louise alone is 4,200 acres. Source: skibig3.com, read 2026-08-20."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 — FCDO, Canada travel advice, Health: \"Dial 911 and ask for an ambulance.\" Read 2026-08-20.","hospital":"Banff Mineral Springs Hospital (Banff townsite) — operational fact, source pin outstanding","activity_note":"ALTITUDE — and the FCDO names this destination by name. Source: https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/canada , Health, verbatim: \"Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Canada, including skiing and hiking destinations in the Canadian Rockies such as Banff and Lake Louise.\" It also names biting insects and ticks, and mpox, as health risks in Canada. Read 2026-08-20.","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/canada","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:02Z","page_updated":"2026-06-02T17:02:41+01:00","source_country":"canada","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"content_ready_by":"2026-03-25","fire_date":"2026-04-01","booking_window_opens":"2026-04-15","event":"2026-06-01","inflection":"Parks Canada shuttle reservation launch, 15 April 2026 08:00 MDT — the moment a Banff summer becomes bookable or does not","peak":"July–August; 2025 peak-summer visitation up 9% and frontcountry campgrounds sold out","note":"Second, softer inflection: 60% of shuttle seats release at 08:00 MDT two days before departure. Source: parks.canada.ca, read 2026-08-20."},"jewels":[{"name":"Moraine Lake at first light","blurb":"Shuttle-only access with 4am and 5am departures; the road is closed to cars all year.","si":"hiking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"1 June – 12 October","commission":"none held — Parks Canada is a government agency","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["hiking"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"destination","hiking":"primary","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Lake Louise Lakeshore","blurb":"On Parks Canada''s own top ten; reached by the Lakeshore shuttle from 15 May.","si":"hiking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"15 May – 12 October","commission":"none held — Parks Canada is a government agency","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["hiking"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"destination","hiking":"primary","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Banff Upper Hot Springs","blurb":"A public thermal pool run by Parks Canada; $19.75 adult, $64.25 family, locker token included.","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","tier":"essential","commission":"none held — Parks Canada is a government agency","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["family","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"evidenced","hiking":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"primary"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Icefields Parkway","blurb":"Parks Canada: \"this 230 km drive winds through glaciers, emerald lakes, and broad sweeping valleys\". A full day out and back.","si":"family","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"May – October","commission":"none held","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["family"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"primary","hiking":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Banff Gondola to the Sulphur Mountain summit","blurb":"An eight-minute ride; a one-way descent is half the price of admission and under-5s are free.","si":"family","when":"year-round","tier":"comfort","commission":"not contracted — Pursuit / Banff Jasper Collection","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["family","hiking"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"primary","hiking":"evidenced","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Johnston Canyon","blurb":"On Parks Canada''s top ten and connected by Roam Public Transit.","si":"hiking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"year-round","commission":"none held","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["hiking"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"destination","hiking":"primary","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Tunnel Mountain summit","blurb":"Parks Canada: \"the 2.4 km trail to this summit provides views across the town and Bow Valley\".","si":"hiking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"May – October","commission":"none held","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["hiking"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"destination","hiking":"primary","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Lake Minnewanka Loop","blurb":"On Parks Canada''s top ten and connected by Roam Public Transit.","si":"family","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"May – October","commission":"none held","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["family"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"primary","hiking":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Banff Legacy Trail","blurb":"Parks Canada: \"29 km of paved paths and roadways from Canmore to the Bow valley Parkway\".","si":"family","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"May – October","commission":"none held","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["family","hiking"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"primary","hiking":"evidenced","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Cave and Basin National Historic Site","blurb":"Where the national park began; first on Parks Canada''s top ten.","si":"culture","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"year-round","commission":"none held — Parks Canada is a government agency","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","family":"destination","hiking":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Banff Park Museum National Historic Site","blurb":"$5.00 adult, $4.50 senior, youth free.","si":"culture","when":"year-round","tier":"essential","commission":"none held — Parks Canada is a government agency","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","family":"destination","hiking":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Vermilion Lakes Drive","blurb":"On Parks Canada''s top ten; a short drive from the townsite.","si":"family","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","when":"year-round","commission":"none held","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["family"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"primary","hiking":"destination","ski":"destination","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":["none"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"SkiBig3 — Sunshine, Lake Louise and Norquay","blurb":"7,948 acres across three areas, 2 gondolas and 32 chairlifts; Sunshine holds the longest non-glacial season in Canada.","si":"ski","when":"early November – late May","tier":"comfort","commission":"not contracted — SkiBig3","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["ski"],"shelf_fit":{"family":"destination","hiking":"destination","ski":"primary","wellness":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the current advisory for Canada, and can I book it?","a":"The UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office publishes travel advice for Canada and names no advisory against travel to any part of the country — its machine-readable alert field is empty — so there is no restriction standing between you and a booking. Its own words on the same page are \"No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide.\" We link the advice and we do not summarise it.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/canada, reviewed 2026-06-02, read 2026-08-20","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Can I just drive to Moraine Lake?","a":"No. Moraine Lake Road is closed to personal vehicles year-round. Access is the Parks Canada shuttle, a licensed commercial operator, a valid government-issued accessible parking placard, or being a registered guest of Moraine Lake Lodge. Free parking is at the Lake Louise Park and Ride, 1 Whitehorn Road.","source":"parks.canada.ca Banff bulletin and shuttle pages, accessed 2026-08-20","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"When do the shuttle seats go on sale, and how do I actually get one?","a":"Reservations for 2026 opened 15 April at 8am MDT and only 40% of seats went that day. The other 60% are released at 8am MDT two days before departure, so a missed launch is not a lost trip. Book through the Parks Canada Reservation Service or 1-877-737-3783. The earliest Moraine Lake departures are 4am and 5am.","source":"parks.canada.ca, Visiting Lake Louise and Moraine Lake, accessed 2026-08-20","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"Does my park pass cover the hot springs, the museum and the shuttle?","a":"No — each is charged separately. Banff Upper Hot Springs is $19.75 adult, $17.25 senior, $17.25 youth 3-17, free under 3 and $64.25 family, with a locker token included; swimsuit rental $5.00 and towel $3.00. The Banff Park Museum National Historic Site is $5.00 adult, $4.50 senior and free for youth. The shuttle is $12.75 adult on top of the reservation fee. All CAD.","source":"parks.canada.ca fee pages for Banff Upper Hot Springs, Banff Park Museum NHS and Banff National Park, accessed 2026-08-20","si_tag":"value"},{"q":"Is it worth coming outside July and August?","a":"Peak-summer visitation rose 9% in 2025 and the frontcountry campgrounds sold out, totalling 292,033 site nights across the year. The shuttle season runs to 12 October and the ski season runs to mid-May at Sunshine, and between those two the park is materially quieter.","source":"Parks Canada, Banff National Park Annual Report 2025, accessed 2026-08-20","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"How long is the drive up the Icefields Parkway?","a":"Parks Canada describes it as \"this 230 km drive winds through glaciers, emerald lakes, and broad sweeping valleys\". It is a full day out and back, not an afternoon.","source":"parks.canada.ca, Banff top ten, accessed 2026-08-20","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"slug":"banff-canada","canonical":"/destination/banff-canada","primary_keyword":"Banff National Park","keywords":["Banff National Park","Moraine Lake shuttle","Lake Louise","Banff park pass","Banff Upper Hot Springs","Icefields Parkway","SkiBig3"],"schema":["Article","FAQPage"],"content_freshness":"2026-08-20","languages":["en","fr"],"language_note":"Every Parks Canada page cited here is published in French by the same authority, so a French edition has a first-party source already.","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/canada","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:02Z","source_updated":"2026-06-02T17:02:41+01:00"}]},"meta_title":"Banff, Canada — the Rockies with a railway town at their feet","meta_description":"What a Banff trip actually requires: Moraine Lake Road is closed to cars year-round, the shuttle is reservation-gated from 15 April, and the park pass does not cover the hot springs. Government prices, sourced and dated."},"booking":{"book_suppressed":false,"authority":"UK FCDO","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/canada","read":"2026-08-20","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","note":"The FCDO names no advisory against travel anywhere in Canada. That is an absence of restriction and never a green badge. No numeric level is assigned on this row.","fcdo":{"posture":"1","_posture_is_ours":"OUR classification of the FCDO''s page, never her booking posture. The FCDO publishes no level and we assign none."}},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["ski","hiking","wellness","family"],"ultra":null,"source_verified":"2026-08-20","hero":{"query":"Banff, Canada"},"orbit":[],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 0),
  ('vancouver-canada', '13A', 'Vancouver', 'Canada', 'Sea, city and mountains at once', 'live', 'stub', 'oceanAerial', null, '{}', '{}', '{}', null, null, null, 1),
  ('alta-utah', '12A', 'Alta', 'United States', 'America''s purist powder', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","culinary","wellness","family","romance","entertainment"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Alta = head of Little Cottonwood Canyon, INDEPENDENT (Ikon Pass PARTNER + Mountain Collective member; Ikon add-on $859 / Ikon Base $359); SKI-ONLY (no snowboarding - one of just three US resorts, with Deer Valley + Mad River Glen)","Both a ski area AND a real incorporated TOWN (~8,560 ft, ~228 residents, founded 1865 silver camp) - one of the highest towns in the US; genuinely high base 8,530 ft / summit 11,068 ft","ONE OF AMERICA''S OLDEST SKI AREAS: Collins chairlift opened Jan 1939 (2nd chairlift in the US after Sun Valley); Alf Engen hired 1935; Sunnyside six-pack (2022) modernization","~2,614 acres, 2,538 ft lift-served vertical, 116+ runs, ~55% advanced-expert; ~500-547 in snow (''Greatest Snow on Earth'', record ~900 in 1982-83); no night skiing","Joint Alta-Snowbird (''Alta-Bird'') ticket since 2002 + Mineral Basin interconnect; classic European-style ski LODGES (Alta Lodge 1940, Rustler 1947 half-board, Snowpine luxe ~2019, Alta Peruvian, Goldminer''s Daughter) - purist lodge culture, NOT a luxury village","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: town-cited ~500k visitors/yr is a CONSENSUS ESTIMATE, not an audited count; heavy SL-valley powder-day day-trips","NO on-site cat/heli - Wasatch Powderbird is a SEPARATE operation (Snowbird/POWDR family), not an Alta product; NO natural hot springs (protected drinking-water watershed - dogs banned; lodge hot tubs man-made); prices dynamic","SLC ~29-32 mi / ~45 min-1 hr via SR-210 (canyon permitting); CANYON SAFETY SPINE: SR-210 winter dead-end + traction law, UDOT avalanche closures, INTERLODGE (official legal indoor confinement via Alta Central - among the most avalanche-managed inhabited places in NA)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (medical/fire/rescue); Town of Alta Marshal''s Office (801) 742-3522 for local law enforcement; alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"No in-canyon hospital - full-service ERs down-canyon in Salt Lake valley (~45 min-1 hr via SR-210, canyon-access permitting); verify nearest facility","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~8,530 ft GENUINELY HIGH - higher than many resorts'' summits; summit ~11,068 ft; real AMS risk for sea-level arrivals - hydrate, ease alcohol, consider a valley night to acclimatise, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE life-safety spine (in-bounds patrolled/controlled; hike-to + backcountry severe) - Utah Avalanche Center (UAC) ''Salt Lake'' region - VERIFY exact zone (UAC page 403); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; NO on-site cat/heli (Powderbird separate); SR-210 winter DEAD-END + traction law + UDOT avalanche closures + INTERLODGE (legal indoor confinement via Alta Central - follow Town/lodge instructions; exact ordinance verify); tree-wells; cold + intense high-elevation UV","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:42Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"Deep winter + storm/powder days (Christmas/NY, Presidents'' Week, any big storm cycle); heavy SL-valley day-trip traffic on powder mornings","shoulder":"early season (Dec), Jan midweek, long high-altitude spring (Apr)","green":"summer + fall (canyon quiets, no lift-served skiing) + Oct-Nov lull","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + the lodges (half-board, limited beds) 3-6 mo; storm-chasing powder trips opportunistic; Alta/Ikon passes by early summer (best-price deadline)","off_season_specials":"long spring skiing; midweek value; lodge half-board packages","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, ML