  ('beaver-creek-colorado', '12A', 'Beaver Creek', 'United States', 'Heated escalators, 3 p', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","family","culinary","entertainment","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Beaver Creek = Vail Resorts / Epic; a PURPOSE-BUILT 1980 luxury resort village (Beaver Creek Village + Bachelor Gulch + Arrowhead) - NOT a historic town; ~10 mi west of Vail","~2,082 acres, ~150 trails, vertical 3,340 ft (base 8,100 / summit 11,440), ~25 lifts; terrain ~19 beg/43 int/38 adv; ~310 in snow + ~605 ac snowmaking; beginner-friendly up top","Signature touches: heated village escalators + free 3 p.m. chocolate-chip cookies daily","Genuine ULTRA bed base: Ritz-Carlton Bachelor Gulch (21,000 sq-ft spa), Park Hyatt Beaver Creek, The Osprey (RockResort, ~26 ft to a chairlift - closest in NA), The Pines Lodge, Beaver Creek Lodge","Dining: Splendido at the Chateau (Michelin-listed) + Beano''s Cabin (snowcat-sleigh dinner)","MARQUEE: Stifel Birds of Prey FIS Alpine World Cup (Birds of Prey course) - largest edition yet 3-13 Dec 2026 (men''s + women''s, 7 races/2 weekends)","NO in-bounds cat- or heli-skiing (guided BC + scenic snowcat/snow-coach to Camp Hale + McCoy Park snowshoe only; CO heli = Telluride/Silverton); NO natural hot springs on-site (Glenwood ~51-60 mi)","EGE ~17 mi (very close); DEN ~130 mi; Vail Health Hospital (Level III trauma, ~20 min) + slopeside Beaver Creek Medical Center; US-TRAFFIC CANDOR ~#11 consensus, not published"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"Vail Health Hospital (Vail, ~20 min) - Level III Trauma Center + helipad; slopeside Beaver Creek Medical Center (outpatient ED of Vail Health)","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~8,100 ft, summit ~11,440 ft - AMS real; acclimatize, hydrate, ease alcohol, de