  ('big-sky-montana', '12A', 'Big Sky', 'United States', 'One of America''s biggest mountains', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","romance","adventure","family","culinary","wellness","entertainment"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Big Sky = Boyne Resorts / Ikon; Lone Peak summit 11,166 ft, base ~7,400-7,500 ft, VERTICAL 4,350 ft; 5,850 acres, 320 trails, 40 lifts (2 gondolas + tram); combines former Moonlight Basin + Spanish Peaks (both acquired 2013) as one resort","The NEW Lone Peak Tram is operational (replaced the 1995 15-passenger tram; replacement announced 2022); all lift tickets include unlimited daily tram access - DO NOT publish old 15-person specs (new capacity/opening date unverified)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: ''Biggest Skiing in America'' (~5,850 ac) is CONTESTED - Park City (~6,700 ac) is the largest lift-served; Boyne calls Big Sky ''second-largest''. Quote acreage, not the superlative. No per-resort skier count published","Terrain ~21% beginner base up to 11% expert + 8% extreme off Lone Peak; ~400 in snow (resort figure; OnTheSnow lists 265 - flag); no night skiing; acreage-per-skier among the most generous in US skiing (uncrowded)","BZN (Bozeman Yellowstone Intl, Montana''s busiest) ~45 mi / ~1 hr N via US-191 Gallatin Canyon; ~midway to West Yellowstone (~45 mi) - a two-season Yellowstone-gateway basecamp","Luxury base: Montage Big Sky (100 rooms, ski access, golf; opening yr verify) + historic Lone Mountain Ranch (all-inclusive guest ranch, 25 cabins, 80+ km Nordic) + Summit Hotel; One&Only Moonlight Basin REPORTED but UNCONFIRMED (verify)","Strong dining scene: Everett''s 8800 (fine dining at 8,800 ft), Peaks Chophouse, M by the Alinea Group (culinary residency), Umbrella Bar (360 glass), Vista Hall food hall","NO on-site cat/heli (lift-served incl tram; backcountry via third-party guides; Nordic at Lone Mountain Ranch); NO natural hot springs at resort (Nor